      "label": "Double speed, double energy",
      "why_tempting": "Most things we know scale in step with speed.",
      "refutation": "Energy is 1/2 m v squared: double the speed means 4 times the energy.",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinetic_energy",
      "source_note": "Page states the correct model; that this mistake is common is unverified"
    },
    {
      "id": "faster-than-square",
      "label": "It explodes even faster",
      "why_tempting": "Once you know it's not linear, it's tempting to overshoot.",
      "refutation": "It grows with the square of speed: 2x speed is 4x energy, not 8x.",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinetic_energy",
